From 1bd11a983d1077425158e61afe3454801dfff28a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PePe Amengual <2208324+jamengual@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:44:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] kubelet: in-place pod resize on FreeBSD

FreeBSD container limits are rctl rules on the container's jail; the
runtime can change them in place (CRI-O UpdateContainerResources ->
'ocijail update', which replaces the rules). Wire up the kubelet side:

- allocation: allow InPlacePodVerticalScaling on FreeBSD (container
  level). Pod-level resources aren't enforced on FreeBSD, so pod-level
  resize stays unsupported (its allocation tests are skipped).
- cm: helpers_freebsd.go with the platform-independent parts of
  helpers_linux.go (CFS shares/quota conversions, ResourceConfigForPod):
  the stubs returned nil/0, so doPodResizeAction failed with 'unable to
  get resource configuration'. cgroupfs functions remain stubs.
- cm: a FreeBSD pod container manager whose GetPodCgroupConfig reports no
  pod-level config and SetPodCgroupConfig is a no-op (no pod cgroup), as
  with the Linux no-op manager; the stub returned 'not implemented'.
- kuberuntime: generateContainerResources returns the same resources as
  container creation; generateUpdatePodSandboxResourcesRequest returns a
  request instead of nil (nil is a resize error); toKubeContainerResources
  converts the runtime-reported resources back, so the kubelet can see the
  resize completed. Round-trip test.
